{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.FuchsianAnalytic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.ODE.Gronwall"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.phiKZ_swap_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.phiKZ_swap_mul","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L225-L251","doc":"**Inversion**: `Φ(B, A) · Φ(A, B) = 1` (Drinfeld (2.12), `Φ(B,A) = Φ(A,B)⁻¹`). The solution\nnormalised at `1` for `(A, B)` is the solution normalised at `0` for `(B, A)` read in `1 − t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.G₁_eq_G₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.G₁_eq_G₀","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L223-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.phiKZ_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.phiKZ_spec","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L216-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.phiKZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.phiKZ","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L210-L213","doc":"`Φ_KZ`, the associator of `kz_associator`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.kz_associator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.kz_associator","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L171-L208","doc":"**The KZ associator.** For residues `A, B` and the normalised formal solutions `H₀` (at `0`,\ncoefficients `kzM0 A B`) and `H₁` (at `1`, coefficients `kzM0 B A`), there is a unique `Φ` with\n`G₀(t) = G₁(t) Φ` on `(0, 1)`, and it is a unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.isUnit_tpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.isUnit_tpow","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L169-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.exists_isUnit_series","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.exists_isUnit_series","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L154-L167","doc":"A convergent series with `H 0 = 1` is a unit for small positive `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.series_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.series_zero","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L149-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.eqOn_mul_of_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.eqOn_mul_of_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L141-L146","doc":"**Connection matrix from one invertible value.** If `G` and `X` solve KZ on `(0, 1)` and\n`G(t*)` is a unit, then `X = G · (G(t*)⁻¹ X(t*))` on `(0, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.eqOn_of_isKZSol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.eqOn_of_isKZSol","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L106-L138","doc":"**Uniqueness for the KZ equation on `(0, 1)`.** Two solutions agreeing at one point of\n`(0, 1)` agree on all of `(0, 1)` (Gronwall). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.norm_kzΩ_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.norm_kzΩ_le","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L93-L103","doc":"`‖Ω(s)‖ ≤ ‖A‖/a + ‖B‖/(1 − b)` for `0 < a < s < b < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.IsKZSol.mul_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.IsKZSol.mul_const","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.isKZSol_G₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.isKZSol_G₁","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L71-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.isKZSol_G₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.isKZSol_G₀","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L67-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.G₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.G₁","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L64-L65","doc":"The solution normalised at `1`: `G₁(t) = H₁(1 − t) (1 − t)^B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.G₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.G₀","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L61-L62","doc":"The solution normalised at `0`: `G₀(t) = H₀(t) t^A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.IsKZSol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.IsKZSol","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L57-L59","doc":"`G` solves the three-point KZ equation `G' = Ω G` on `(0, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.kzΩ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.AssociatorKZ.kzΩ","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/AssociatorKZ.lean#L54-L55","doc":"The KZ connection coefficient `Ω(t) = t⁻¹ A + (t − 1)⁻¹ B`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}